   553	/**
   554	 * B-3ddc: render the honest unavailable reason `turn_failed(<digest>)` for a
   555	 * scanned failure event. The digest is a short sanitized excerpt of the
   556	 * error message — deliberately human-readable (not a hash) so the ledger row
   557	 * itself names the failure:
   558	 *   - null/empty (after trim) message -> 'no_error_message';
   559	 *   - a message that itself parses as a JSON object (the observed B-3928
   560	 *     payload string-encodes a nested 400 body) is drilled to the INNERMOST
   561	 *     `error.message` string (bounded depth; falls back to the original
   562	 *     message when nothing extractable is found);
   563	 *   - control characters (\n \r \t, NUL, DEL) and whitespace runs collapse to
   564	 *     a single space; the result is hard-capped at
